---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

const description =
  'What VibeLocked collects. This static site uses cookie-free GoatCounter analytics. The newsletter runs on Buttondown.';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description={description} path="/privacy">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="kicker">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This version of the site is a folder of static files. It does not have accounts. It counts visits with GoatCounter, which sets no cookies.
      </p>
    </header>
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        Reading the site does not create an account. Pages do not embed advertising pixels or social trackers. The theme button stores your light or dark choice in <code>localStorage</code> on your device. That is not a cookie, and it is not sent to us.
      </p>
      <h2>Newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        The newsletter is sent with <a href="https://buttondown.com">Buttondown</a>. When you sign up, Buttondown stores your email address, the date you subscribed, and basic delivery data such as opens and clicks. You must confirm your address before you receive anything. Every issue has a one-click unsubscribe link, and you can ask us to delete your address at any time. We do not sell or share the list. See the <a href="https://buttondown.com/legal/privacy">Buttondown privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com">GoatCounter</a> to count page views. It sets no cookies and does not track you across sites. For each view it records the page path, the referring page, the browser and operating system, screen size, and an approximate country. It does not store your IP address or build a profile of you. A short-lived hash is used only to avoid counting the same visit twice. See the <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/help/privacy">GoatCounter privacy policy</a>. Blocking the script with a content blocker does not affect how the site works.
      </p>
      <h2>Repo scanner</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/scan">scanner</a> runs in your browser. When you scan a repo, your browser requests the file list and file contents directly from GitHub (api.github.com and raw.githubusercontent.com), so GitHub sees that request like any other visit. The repo URL and the results are not sent to VibeLocked and are not stored. The scanner only reads public repos and never asks for a token or a login.
      </p>
      <h2>Email you send us</h2>
      <p>
        If you write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.helloEmail}`}>{SITE.helloEmail}</a> or <a href={`mailto:${SITE.sponsorEmail}`}>{SITE.sponsorEmail}</a>, we use the message to reply and, for sponsor mail, to discuss a placement. We do not sell that correspondence.
      </p>
      <h2>Hosting logs</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted as static files on GitHub Pages. GitHub may keep ordinary request logs, including IP addresses, as part of serving the files. VibeLocked does not add its own logging on top.
      </p>
      <h2>Links</h2>
      <p>
        Guides link to official vendor documentation. Those sites have their own policies. Sponsor and affiliate links, when a placement exists, will be labeled on the page. There are no paid or affiliate links on the site right now.
      </p>
      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        The site is written for people building software. It is not directed at children.
      </p>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the page will change with it. The meaningful version is the one published at this URL.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.helloEmail}`}>{SITE.helloEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
